#: src/shell.md:1
msgid "Shell"
msgstr ""

#: src/shell.md:3
msgid ""
"The `shell` setting controls the command used to invoke recipe lines and "
"backticks. Shebang recipes are unaffected. The default shell is `sh -cu`."
msgstr ""

#: src/shell.md:6
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# use python3 to execute recipe lines and backticks\n"
"set shell := [\"python3\", \"-c\"]\n"
"\n"
"# use print to capture result of evaluation\n"
"foos := `print(\"foo\" * 4)`\n"
"\n"
"foo:\n"
"  print(\"Snake snake snake snake.\")\n"
"  print(\"{{foos}}\")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/shell.md:18
msgid ""
"`just` passes the command to be executed as an argument. Many shells will "
"need an additional flag, often `-c`, to make them evaluate the first "
"argument."
msgstr ""

#: src/shell.md:21
msgid "Windows Shell"
msgstr ""

#: src/shell.md:23
msgid ""
"`just` uses `sh` on Windows by default. To use a different shell on Windows, "
"use the `[windows]` attribute on the `shell` setting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/shell.md:26
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"[windows]\n"
"set shell := [\"powershell.exe\", \"-NoLogo\", \"-Command\"]\n"
"\n"
"hello:\n"
"  Write-Host \"Hello, world!\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/shell.md:34
msgid ""
"See [powershell.just](https://github.com/casey/just/blob/master/examples/"
"powershell.just) for a justfile that uses PowerShell on all platforms."
msgstr ""

